From: synman <1299716+synman@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] drm/xe/oc: log PCODE mailbox failures and stop faking a mem_speed read

Applies on top of exzile/intel-arc-pro-fan-control's xe_gt_oc.c (commit
0fc18ceefbc5b6ff341926745f95f7c47058a741) on the Debian 7.2.9 xe tree.

- xe_pcode.c: print the raw PCODE status beside the decoded error, so a
  failed mailbox call says which status the firmware returned.
- vf_curve end: warn when the finalize call fails. The return path is
  unchanged.
- mem_speed read: PCODE answers -EPROTO until a rate has been staged
  since boot. Return that error instead of reporting a guessed stock
  rate, so userspace can tell "unknown" from "19000".
- mem_speed commit: log every commit result and return its error, so a
  rejected write is visible in dmesg and to the writer.

Seen on an Arc Pro B70 (8086:e223, subsystem 1849:6025): with nothing
staged, every boot logs "PCODE Mailbox failed: -71 Unknown (status 0x8)"
once per mem_speed read. That line is expected.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_gt_oc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_gt_oc.c
@@ -168,7 +168,10 @@
 			return ret;
 	}
 
-	xe_pcode_read(tile, OC_MBOX_END, &end0, &end1);
+	ret = xe_pcode_read(tile, OC_MBOX_END, &end0, &end1);
+	if (ret)
+		drm_warn(&xe->drm, "oc: vf_curve end ret=%d data0=%#x data1=%#x\n",
+			 ret, end0, end1);
 
 	return count;
 }
@@ -184,10 +187,10 @@
 	guard(xe_pm_runtime)(xe);
 
 	/* p1=5 read returns -EPROTO until a value has been staged (fresh boot =
-	 * hardware default); report the stock speed in that case. */
+	 * hardware default); return that error so the caller sees nothing is staged. */
 	ret = xe_pcode_read(tile, OC_MBOX_MEM_READ, &mbps, &hi);
 	if (ret)
-		mbps = OC_MEM_STOCK_MBPS;
+		return ret;
 
 	return sysfs_emit(buf, "%u\n", mbps);
 }
@@ -211,7 +214,11 @@
 	ret = xe_pcode_write64_timeout(tile, OC_MBOX_MEM_SET, mbps, 0, 1);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
-	xe_pcode_read(tile, OC_MBOX_MEM_COMMIT, &c0, &c1);   /* commit / finalize */
+	ret = xe_pcode_read(tile, OC_MBOX_MEM_COMMIT, &c0, &c1);   /* commit / finalize */
+	drm_info(&xe->drm, "oc: mem_speed %u commit ret=%d data0=%#x data1=%#x\n",
+		 mbps, ret, c0, c1);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
 
 	return count;
 }
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_pcode.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_pcode.c
@@ -57,8 +57,8 @@
 	}
 
 	if (err) {
-		drm_err(&tile_to_xe(tile)->drm, "PCODE Mailbox failed: %d %s",
-			err_decode, err_str);
+		drm_err(&tile_to_xe(tile)->drm, "PCODE Mailbox failed: %d %s (status %#x)",
+			err_decode, err_str, err);
 
 		return err_decode;
 	}
